 ## Background
-The method is based on Garrity's algorithm for tracing rays through tetrahedral grids by determining the exit face and following neighbor pointers [S1, book]. Weiler et al. implemented this approach on a GPU, storing vertex and adjacency data in texture memory to enable fast, concurrent mesh traversal [S1, book][S2, unofficial]. It is cited as a promising concept for volume-based rendering of tetrahedral data [S2, unofficial].
